# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# Only third-party allocations that mkpool cannot free belong here. Never add a
# suppression for our own code: the point of running LSan is to catch that.

# libpqxx builds type-name strings in its own static initialisers -- the stack is
# demangle_type_name() called from ld.so's dl_init, before main() -- and never
# frees them. 134 bytes, once per process, entirely inside libpqxx-7.10.so.
# Nothing in mkpool holds a pointer to them, so there is nothing we could free.
# Without this, every ASan job fails on a leak in a library we do not control.
leak:libpqxx
